# Tracker Brief Viewer — agent sandbox

## Rule

When running `open-brief-viewer.js` or `tracker-feed-render.js --open` from a **Cursor agent Shell**, always pass **`required_permissions: ["all"]`**.

The opener calls `cursor --open-url` to hand off to the local `entrata.tracker-brief-opener` extension. That CLI writes under `~/Library/Application Support/Cursor/logs/`. The default agent sandbox returns **EPERM** and Simple Browser never opens — the script now exits **1** with an explicit sandbox message.

## Commands

```bash
node initiative-1-tracker/tracker/scripts/tracker-feed-render.js --open
# or
npm run brief:open-viewer --prefix initiative-1-tracker/tracker
```

Both require Shell **`required_permissions: ["all"]`** when invoked by an agent.

## If exit 1

Output includes `auto-open blocked — agent sandbox`. Retry the same command with `all`. URL is copied to clipboard — manual fallback: Cmd+Shift+P → Simple Browser: Show → Cmd+V.
